# Documents, fragments, commands, and streams

**Prerequisites:** [first app](/docs/tutorials/first-app/).
**Kind:** concept.
**Next:** [Update the UI](/docs/how-to/update-the-ui/) or
[Runtime](/docs/reference/runtime/).

Rocci treats HTML as the shared boundary. JavaScript enhances; it is not the
unit of composition.

| Handler | Typical result | Browser behavior |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `@get:view(path)` | Complete HTML document | Load or navigate |
| `@get:fragment(path)` | Fragment with a stable target | One-shot read/morph |
| `@post:fragment(path)` | Fragment with a stable target | One-shot mutation/morph |
| `@post:command(path)` | No representation (`{}` body) | Empty SSE for Datastar; 204 otherwise |
| `@get:live(path)` | Shared fragment | Long-lived SSE; subscribed tabs morph |

The mutation roles also admit PUT, PATCH, and DELETE. Live paths are plural;
use one coherence stream when possible, and explicit subscriptions when a
module has more than one. Do not patch the same `id` from both a finite
fragment and a stream.

Canonical comparison: [Counter](/examples/counter/) versus
[Live counter](/examples/live-counter/).

**Related:** [Datastar as transport](/docs/concepts/datastar-as-transport/).
